First, I need to recall the formula for calcium correction.  
From what I remember, the formula adjusts the serum calcium based on the albumin level because calcium binds to proteins in the blood, mainly albumin.  
When albumin levels are low, more calcium is free, which can make the total calcium appear lower.  
The formula is: Corrected Calcium = Measured Calcium + (4 - Albumin).  
