Wait, actually, the formula is: Corrected Calcium (mg/dL) = Measured Calcium (mg/dL) + (4.0 - Albumin (g/dL)).  
Another way to calculate it is: Corrected Ca = Measured Ca + (4 - Alb).  
For example, if someone has 10 mg/dL calcium and albumin of 3.5, corrected would be 10 + (4 - 3.5) = 10.5.  
If albumin is 3.0, then 10 + 1 = 11.  
So the formula works.  
